This file lists third-party material that ships in this ADW Lite copy, and the
sources that its rules derive from. Each entry names the source, its license
as stated upstream, and the files of this copy that carry it. The MIT license
in LICENSE covers the rest of this copy. engine/SOURCE.json names the upstream
revision. The upstream repository ships more files than this copy, such as
the German rule modules, the exemplar corpora and the evals folder. This copy
carries none of them, and the entries below say so where it matters.


1. humanizer-de 5.28.1

The source is https://github.com/marmbiz/humanizer-de at tag v5.28.1, by
Martin Moeller. Portions of it derive from blader/humanizer by Siqi Chen.

humanizer-de ships its scripts and original material under MIT. It ships
references/patterns.md and the matching pattern tables under CC BY-SA 4.0.
Those tables adapt the Wikipedia project pages "Anzeichen für KI-generierte
Inhalte" (German) and "Signs of AI writing" (English). The humanizer-de
NOTICE file states this split.

We wrote all rule descriptions in our own words (decision Q13). These files
of this copy follow a humanizer-de pattern.

  engine/lib/markup.py, the thematic break checks, Muster 57 cases A to C
  engine/lib/parataxis.py, the run of bare main clauses, pattern 51

The upstream German rule modules with the borrowed trigger lists
(german_rules/chatbot.py, format.py, markup.py, phrases.py, rhetoric.py,
semantic_claims.py and words.py) do not ship here. engine/lib/german_rules
holds only the rule loader.


2. German style books, rules in our own words

The upstream German rules restate points from these books in our own words.
No sentence from them ships in this copy.

  Monika Salchert, Verständliches Schreiben. Selbstlernheft. Bundesakademie
  für öffentliche Verwaltung im Bundesministerium des Innern (BAköV),
  2nd edition, September 2012.

  Andreas Baumert, Professionell texten. dtv Ratgeber, C.H. Beck.

  Stefan Gottschling, Einfach besser texten. GABAL, 2006.


3. Duden

The source is Dudenredaktion, Einfach können. Rechtschreibung,
Zeichensetzung und Grammatik. Cornelsen, 2025. ISBN 978-3-411-75696-4.

engine/lib/german_punctuation.py and engine/lib/catalog_de.py restate German
typography rules in our own words. These cover the Gedankenstrich, the
Bis-Strich, the Ergänzungsstrich, German quotation marks, the ellipsis, and
the genitive apostrophe. No Duden text ships.


4. Exemplar sentences and label files

The upstream repository keeps German and English exemplar sentences
(pattern_exemplars_de.jsonl, pattern_exemplars_de.json and
pattern_exemplars.jsonl) and rater label files under evals/. They quote
German and English Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL), Project Gutenberg
through sedthh/gutenberg_multilang (MIT for the collection), WildChat 4.8M
(ODC-BY), the lmarena arena-human-preference-100k set (CC BY 4.0 for user
prompts, provider terms for model outputs), the COLING 2025 GenAI Content
Detection Task 1 data (Apache-2.0 for the task repository) and local
Wikipedia, Gutenberg and CNN_DailyMail files. None of these files ship in
this copy.


5. German Wiktionary

The upstream evals/syllable_counter.json measures the syllable counter of
engine/lib/german_syllables.py against the Worttrennung field of
https://de.wiktionary.org (CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL). That file does not ship
in this copy, and engine/lib/german_syllables.py stores no Wiktionary text.


6. Principle sources

engine/lib/principle_kb.py reads principles.sqlite from the cache folder of
the plugin data home when the file exists. Upstream builds that file at
install from DevIQ (https://github.com/NimblePros/deviq-hugo at commit
2c5341047e6cf62bc0598dd3cdc2f55951cd125a) and programming-principles
(https://github.com/webpro/programming-principles at commit
a0c299c981cc31f4d4bd5c265cba80d3e9471429). Neither repository carries a
license file, see upstream. This copy ships no downloader and no text from
them.

STE100 detectors

The detectors use ADW masking. Only the rule ideas and the modal-perfect expression come from scripts/ste-lint.py in danyuchn/asd-ste100-skill at commit 7073627.

